3. What is a vocabulary?
A vocabulary is the collection of tokens a particular tokenizer knows how to represent, each associated with an ID.
Token	Example ID
loan	201
customer	502
bank	134
?	12

The tokenizer uses its vocabulary to convert text into token IDs. The model then uses its learned parameters to process the resulting sequence.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vocabulary: the available token units and their mappings.
Token ID: the integer associated with a token.
Embedding: the vector representation looked up or derived using the token ID.

#Different models can use different tokenizers and vocabularies
