What are special tokens?
Special tokens are dedicated tokens used by a model or tokenizer to represent structural information, such as message boundaries, turn endings, or other control signals.

Why are they important?
In an agentic application, the model may need to distinguish between a normal answer and a request to call a tool. Message structure and control markers help supported model formats represent these differences.
Don't manually add special tokens unless the model's documentation or task requires them. Tokenizers and chat APIs often handle the relevant formatting for you.
